# PlasticOS Capability Type Policy

**Scope:** `plasticos_facility_profile`. Facility evidence and projections stay in Odoo. Scoring semantics stay with CEG/EIE through Gate.

## Rule: capability changes stay inside the Odoo projection

Adding capability types to `capability_type_data.xml` without the Odoo projection is prohibited. `plasticos.equipment.type` and the facility `has_*` flags are retired (ADR-134).

### Required steps for a new capability type

1. Add seed data in `data/capability_type_data.xml`.
2. Add the type's detail fields on `plasticos.capability` when the type carries details.
3. Add the capability to the emitted facility packet.
4. Add a test of that Odoo projection.

### Anti-pattern

```xml
<!-- WRONG: data-only addition creates an orphaned capability -->
<record id="cap_new_machine" model="plasticos.capability.type">
  <field name="name">New Machine</field>
  <field name="code">new_machine</field>
</record>
```

### Correct wiring pattern

```python
# capability.py — one line of the new type on the facility profile
{"capability_type_id": new_type.id, "details": {"line_count": 1}}

# intake facility packet
{"code": line.capability_type_id.code, "name": line.capability_type_id.name}
```

## Rationale

- The facility packet is the Odoo projection of what the site can do.
- An unseeded code never becomes a capability line.
- Data-only additions skip that projection.
